**Key analysis:** For both lines and circles, "equidistant from all four" means each point is at the same distance $t \geq 0$ from the path. This partitions the four points into two groups (those at signed distance $+t$ and $-t$). I need to count, over all partitions into two non-empty groups, the paths that realize each partition — showing each partition yields exactly one path.

